1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:01,734
Wagtail Unboxed.

2
00:00:01,734 --> 00:00:03,550
Learning by building.

3
00:00:04,350 --> 00:00:05,943
That is a real website.

4
00:00:05,943 --> 00:00:10,028
And that is somebody editing it, without touching any code.

5
00:00:10,028 --> 00:00:14,945
By the end of this series you will have built it, from an empty folder,

6
00:00:14,945 --> 00:00:17,784
and you will understand every file in it.

7
00:00:18,584 --> 00:00:20,482
So, what is Wagtail?

8
00:00:20,482 --> 00:00:25,226
It is a content management system built on Django.

9
00:00:26,026 --> 00:00:30,516
It is not a fork of Django, and it is not a competitor to it.

10
00:00:30,516 --> 00:00:34,049
It is a set of Django apps that you pip install.

11
00:00:34,049 --> 00:00:35,816
Models are still models.

12
00:00:35,816 --> 00:00:38,024
Templates are still templates.

13
00:00:38,024 --> 00:00:43,103
What Wagtail adds is a page tree, a genuinely good editing interface,

14
00:00:43,103 --> 00:00:47,740
an image system, and a content block system called StreamField.

15
00:00:48,540 --> 00:00:54,305
If you already write Django, you already know about seventy percent of Wagtail.

16
00:00:54,305 --> 00:00:57,078
This series is about the other thirty.

17
00:00:57,878 --> 00:00:59,101
Who is this for?

18
00:00:59,101 --> 00:01:00,095
Three groups.

19
00:01:00,095 --> 00:01:05,218
Django developers who keep getting asked, can the client edit this.

20
00:01:05,218 --> 00:01:11,488
Agency and freelance developers, building sites for people who are not developers.

21
00:01:11,488 --> 00:01:13,706
And people leaving WordPress,

22
00:01:13,706 --> 00:01:18,752
who want that editing experience without the PHP plugin ecosystem.

23
00:01:19,552 --> 00:01:23,218
Now the part I am not going to soften.

24
00:01:24,018 --> 00:01:25,881
You need basic Python.

25
00:01:25,881 --> 00:01:28,675
Functions, classes, imports, pip.

26
00:01:28,675 --> 00:01:30,368
And you need Django.

27
00:01:30,368 --> 00:01:34,009
Models, migrations, templates, settings.py.

28
00:01:34,009 --> 00:01:38,835
That is the real prerequisite, because Wagtail is Django.

29
00:01:38,835 --> 00:01:42,561
Plus enough HTML and CSS to edit a template,

30
00:01:42,561 --> 00:01:47,556
and enough command line to run a command and read an error.

31
00:01:48,356 --> 00:01:52,422
If models.py and make migrations are not familiar yet,

32
00:01:52,422 --> 00:01:56,638
pause this video and go do the official Django tutorial.

33
00:01:56,638 --> 00:01:58,896
It is about a weekend of work.

34
00:01:58,896 --> 00:02:00,026
Then come back.

35
00:02:00,026 --> 00:02:02,585
You will get far more out of this,

36
00:02:02,585 --> 00:02:08,006
and you will not spend fourteen episodes copying code you cannot change.

37
00:02:08,806 --> 00:02:14,438
What you do not need: any prior Wagtail, any prior CMS experience,

38
00:02:14,438 --> 00:02:17,766
no front end frameworks, and no Docker.

39
00:02:17,766 --> 00:02:20,752
Wagtail itself is taught from zero.

40
00:02:21,552 --> 00:02:22,945
One practical note.

41
00:02:22,945 --> 00:02:28,297
I record on Windows, so Windows commands are what you will see on screen.

42
00:02:28,297 --> 00:02:34,383
Every episode ships a commands file in the repo with the mac and Linux equivalents.

43
00:02:34,383 --> 00:02:37,242
Nothing in this series is Windows only.

44
00:02:38,042 --> 00:02:39,506
Here is the plan.

45
00:02:39,506 --> 00:02:42,348
Fourteen episodes, in three acts.

46
00:02:42,348 --> 00:02:47,601
One concept per episode, fifteen to twenty five minutes each,

47
00:02:47,601 --> 00:02:50,012
and nothing gets hand waved.

48
00:02:50,812 --> 00:02:53,381
Act one, episodes one to three.

49
00:02:53,381 --> 00:02:54,127
Unboxing.

50
00:02:54,127 --> 00:03:00,426
We create the project, and then we read every single file Wagtail generated.

51
00:03:00,426 --> 00:03:02,415
All twenty nine of them.

52
00:03:02,415 --> 00:03:08,134
Most tutorials skip that, and it is exactly why people stay confused.

53
00:03:08,934 --> 00:03:11,838
Act two, episodes four to eleven.

54
00:03:11,838 --> 00:03:12,630
We build.

55
00:03:12,630 --> 00:03:18,791
Templates and static files, StreamField, images and documents, a blog,

56
00:03:18,791 --> 00:03:24,600
reusable snippets, navigation, a working contact form, and search.

57
00:03:25,400 --> 00:03:28,754
And act three, episodes twelve to fourteen.

58
00:03:28,754 --> 00:03:29,456
Shipping.

59
00:03:29,456 --> 00:03:35,150
Polishing the editor experience for the client, real production settings,

60
00:03:35,150 --> 00:03:37,802
and deploying to an actual domain.

61
00:03:38,602 --> 00:03:40,897
Everything is in a public repo.

62
00:03:40,897 --> 00:03:43,265
Every episode ends on a git tag.

63
00:03:43,265 --> 00:03:49,261
So if you want to start at episode seven, you check out the tag from episode six,

64
00:03:49,261 --> 00:03:53,332
and you have exactly the code that episode begins with.

65
00:03:54,132 --> 00:03:56,705
The database is not in the repo.

66
00:03:56,705 --> 00:04:00,404
You make your own content as you follow along.

67
00:04:00,404 --> 00:04:01,932
That is deliberate.

68
00:04:01,932 --> 00:04:06,918
Actually making content is how the admin stops being abstract.

69
00:04:07,718 --> 00:04:10,069
And what this series is not.

70
00:04:10,069 --> 00:04:12,421
It is not a Django tutorial.

71
00:04:12,421 --> 00:04:14,856
It is not a front end course.

72
00:04:14,856 --> 00:04:19,727
There is no React, no Tailwind, and no Node, at any point.

73
00:04:19,727 --> 00:04:24,934
We write plain CSS by hand so the episodes stay about Wagtail.

74
00:04:24,934 --> 00:04:27,873
It is not a headless or API series.

75
00:04:27,873 --> 00:04:32,492
And it is not a clone the repo and you are done series.

76
00:04:32,492 --> 00:04:34,424
You will type the code.

77
00:04:35,224 --> 00:04:40,123
Versions are pinned, so the code on screen is the code you get.

78
00:04:40,123 --> 00:04:45,488
Wagtail seven point four point three, Django six point one point one,

79
00:04:45,488 --> 00:04:47,509
Python three point twelve.

80
00:04:47,509 --> 00:04:49,142
Wagtail eight is out.

81
00:04:49,142 --> 00:04:54,352
We are on seven point four on purpose: wider package compatibility,

82
00:04:54,352 --> 00:04:56,218
and it ages more slowly.

83
00:04:57,018 --> 00:05:00,049
Next episode, we set up your machine.

84
00:05:00,049 --> 00:05:03,163
Python, git, and virtual environments.

85
00:05:03,163 --> 00:05:08,079
But if you already have Python, a virtualenv habit, and git,

86
00:05:08,079 --> 00:05:11,683
then skip it and go straight to episode one.

87
00:05:11,683 --> 00:05:13,404
I will see you there.

88
00:05:14,204 --> 00:05:16,055
Thanks for watching.

89
00:05:16,055 --> 00:05:18,553
Everything is linked below.

90
00:05:18,553 --> 00:05:20,404
Let us open the box.
